The `last-input` recording isn't included. Writing to a shared store needs `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, which the `with` clause (`Clock`, `HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>`, `Notifier<'digest'>`) doesn't grant. Importing it would go beyond the node's authority, and the component would likely be rejected at linking. To get this, add a `StateHandle<'…', read-write>` to the node's `with` clause in the graph, then add the import and one `put` call. The output (`seconds`, `fetched`, `notified`) would not change.

If the notifier refuses the message, the node traps instead of returning `notified: false`. That way it never produces an output that breaks `ensures notified == true`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;
    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        // Read the clock once.
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        // One permitted fetch. A transport failure is a value (counted as zero
        // characters); a host outside the allowlist traps at the boundary.
        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => u32::try_from(body.chars().count()).unwrap_or(u32::MAX),
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        let message = format!(
            "heartbeat: t={} feed={} fetched={} chars",
            seconds, feed_url, fetched
        );

        // The contract requires notified == true. Retry once; if the notifier
        // still refuses, trap rather than emit an output violating the contract.
        let notified = notifier::notify(&message) || notifier::notify(&message);
        if !notified {
            panic!("notifier refused the heartbeat notification");
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

